        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0274" n="202" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg202"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5315/487.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the British
                    Ambassador.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-09-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September 11, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Replying to your telegram [note] of September 8, Government of United States
                    appreciates interest and friendly disposition of His Majesty’s Government in
                    respect to American participation in the proposed Chinese railway loan.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, however, to advise Your Excellency that previous to the receipt
                    of Your Excellency’s message, the Government of United States had communicated
                    to the Chinese Government terms and conditions upon which the Government of
                    United States would be willing that American interests should participate in
                    that loan, and that therefore, while these propositions are pending, Government
                    of United States is not prepared to take any action upon the friendly
                    suggestions of the British Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
